# String, list, dictionary, file, and shell builtins

A Text named greeting exists.
greeting is (Uppercase "hello prose").
Print greeting.

A Text named piece exists.
piece is (Substr "abcdef" 2 3).
Print piece.

A List named letters exists.
letters contains "c", "a", and "b".
Print (Sort letters).
Print (Join letters ",").

A Dictionary named capitals exists.
Inside capitals, "France" maps to "Paris".
Inside capitals, "Japan" maps to "Tokyo".
Print (Keys capitals).
Print (Haskey capitals "France").

Write "line1" to the file "_esh_tmp.txt".
Append "line2" to the file "_esh_tmp.txt".
Print (Cat "_esh_tmp.txt").
Print (Fileexists "_esh_tmp.txt").
Print (Isfile "_esh_tmp.txt").
Delete the file "_esh_tmp.txt".

out is `echo shell-ok`.
Print out.
